ne comment accurately describes what was wrong and what the fix should be, so I'll leave it as-is. Now formatting this as JSON with proper escaping for the newlines and quotes in the docstring.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"code\": \"    def should_allow_probe(self) -> bool:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Allow a probe request in the half-open state if under the limit.\\n\\n        BUG_42: the comparison is inverted, allowing probes when the count\\n        has already exceeded the maximum and blocking them when under the limit.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        if self.probe_count < self.max_probes:  # BUG_42: should be < not >\\n            self.probe_count += 1\\n            return True\\n        return False\",\n  \"comments\": \"Corrected the comparison operator in the probe limit check from > to < so probes are permitted only when under the maximum threshold.\"\n}\n```","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4666,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4666},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cfb32158-03d4-414c-9a7e-af7e0b696297","uuid":"53eacfbf-3e89-4544-918f-aab9cd445fb4"}
